# Every service image builds from the repo root, so this is the only
# .dockerignore Docker reads — the ones under frontend/ and new-backend/ apply
# to their own context only and no image uses those contexts anymore.
#
# Why root context: every service's go.mod replaces the shared module with a
# path outside its own directory (new-backend/shared/), which a per-service
# context cannot reach. One root context with repo-root-relative COPY paths is
# the only layout that builds.
#
# Without the exclusions below a local `make deploy` would hand the daemon the
# entire 1.2 GB worktree; a fresh clone is ~5 MB.

.git/
.github/
.idea/
.claude/

# No image consumes these: mobile is Expo-only, scripts/ is host tooling.
mobile/
scripts/
*.md

# Dependency and build trees — restored inside the image, never copied in.
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
**/bin/
**/main
**/*_bin

# Secrets and local noise.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.log
**/coverage.out
**/coverage.html
